title: 'pallet-psm: keep the minimum balance in the reserve on redeem'

doc:
  - audience: Runtime Dev
    description: |
      `redeem` pays the external asset out with `Preservation::Expendable`. A payout that left
      the reserve with a nonzero balance below the asset's minimum balance also paid that rest
      to the caller, so the remaining debt had no reserve. If debt remains and the payout would
      leave such a rest, `redeem` now pays out less, so that the minimum balance stays in the
      reserve. The internal amount that is not redeemed stays with the caller. The redemption
      never fails because of this rule. `Redeemed::external_received` now reports the amount
      that the transfer actually paid.

crates:
  - name: pallet-psm
    bump: patch
